@@OLD
and a fault injected into each member parser fails its operation closed with its exact diagnostic. Removing the pin, an entry script's early load, the restore, the caller-value record or any status read fails a fixture with an exact diagnostic. The contract and the kernel comment say the harness runs its own parsing under `LC_ALL=C`, gives the caller's `LC_ALL` back to the command it captures, and never lets a parse failure read as a pass.
@@NEW
and a fault injected into each member parser fails its operation closed with its exact diagnostic. The kit's suites set `TMPDIR` to the physical path of the directory it names when they start (`/tmp` when it is unset), so its spelling (a trailing or doubled slash, `.` or `..`, a symlink) cannot decide a verdict that compares a path under it, and a `TMPDIR` naming no directory stops a suite by name. Removing the pin, an entry script's early load, the restore, the caller-value record, any status read or the `TMPDIR` canonicalization fails a fixture with an exact diagnostic. The contract and the kernel comment say the harness runs its own parsing under `LC_ALL=C`, gives the caller's `LC_ALL` back to the command it captures, and never lets a parse failure read as a pass, and that the spelling of `TMPDIR` can decide a check that compares a path under it, which the kit's suites pin.
@@END
